Z||000000||Adrift||09-18-2001||12:59 AM||||I'm planning on dying my carpets black, and was wondering if I should bleach them before I dye them? Will this importve the final product?<BR>Thanks<BR>Ari||||reg||5
Z||000001||JayUSA77||09-18-2001||01:28 AM||||do yourself a big favor go on ebay and buy the carpet for 109 bucks its super high quality but make sure its made by ACC.  They custom fit it for your car.  Well worth it.<BR>j<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Adrift||09-18-2001||01:43 AM||||they way I see it why spend $170 CAN when I can try to dye them for next to nothing? What do I have to lose? So, bleach then dye or just dye?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||09-18-2001||02:21 AM||||Real automotive carpet dye should dye right over any color--especially since your're going to use black.  Spray can cr@p rubs off...don't bother.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Spiff||09-18-2001||10:04 AM||||I just bought the carpet off of E-Bay. It was sold by A1 Automotive, and made by ACC. It is the best thing I did. The carpet looks great and was not that expensive. If the dye job doesn't work. I would seriously buy the carpet kit.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ambush||09-18-2001||10:10 AM||||If your gong to Dye the carpet. You need to get the material VERY HOT. Beleive me, it's not going to work. You are going to spend about $30 in dye then do it again because it's almost the color you want. After the second try it doesn't get any better and you may or may no try again. That's $90.00 just buy new carpet. But if you MUST do it yourself...Bleach the carpet first. DO NOT USE BLEACH !!!(Like CLOROX) They have other bleach type products that will assist the dying process.<BR>Note: the carpet is made up a few materials one of which is nylon. the nylon will noty change color||||reg||1
Z||000006||Adrift||09-18-2001||07:29 PM||||I spent $7 at Canadian Tire on a bottle of Spray dye - the way I see it I would throw out the carpet anyways if it didn't work so what did I have to lose? Here are the results:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/floormats.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||rockcrawl||09-18-2001||07:41 PM||||I've used the black spray dye on Fiero carpet. It changed back to brown pretty quickly. That stuff just rubs off. It does work pretty well on the dash and door panels, etc..||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ambush||09-19-2001||09:52 AM||||$7? wow Canada must have some great deals. Let me know how it looks in to months. If t works I going ot invest.||||reg||1
